  "tap_position_0_is_the_control": "the same device taps, the same oracle forward, read at position 0 instead: cosine 0.9999975 at the tap that collapses to 0.8949 at position 7, and no step anywhere through layer 4. So the difference is not in the weights, the lowering, the dtype or the tap machinery -- all of those are shared -- it is in what layer 2's attention does with a position that has predecessors.",
  "what_it_does_not_settle": [
    "WHICH operator inside layer 2's attention: the taps bracket the whole sublayer -- compressed-KV write and read, the sparse attention itself, the output projection and hc_post are all inside the bracket",
    "whether the same site explains the 32-token pinned workload's disagreement, whose gold comes from a comparator that does not reproduce itself past position 7"
  ],
  "why_the_pairing_needs_no_matching": "the vendor's Block does ``x = self.hc_pre(x, pre_mix)`` and then ``x = self.attn_norm(x)``, and the device's IR names a kernel ``main.layerNN.attention.norm`` whose input is ``main.layerNN.hyper_connection.attention.collapsed``. Those are the same tensor, so tap 2k pairs with layers[k].attn_norm by construction. The pairing is CHECKED rather than assumed: tap 0 comes back max|diff| EXACTLY ZERO and cosine 1.0000000000, which no accidental pairing of 5120-element rows produces."
